npm tarball, Chrome CRX, VSIX\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Package Deal' pun read as software packages. Separate fmts: nupkg (alias nuget): zip with `*.nuspec` (XML ns varies) id, version, authors, description, dependencies (JSON id@range), tags; `[Content_Types].xml` + `_rels/.rels` + `package/services/metadata/core-properties/*.psmdcp` creator. wheel (aliases whl, python_wheel): `*.dist-info/METADATA` (RFC 822: Name, Version, Summary, Author, Requires-Dist JSON list), `W\n  {\"id\": \"gate-allowlist-dfir-libs\", \"concept\": \"Prebuild gate refuses installed DFIR libs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS lacks Evtx, regipy, olefile, oletools, dnfile, LnkParse3, lief, cryptography, asn1crypto, dpkt, PIL, sqlite3, wave, ordlookup. Targets evtx-records (python-evtx) and regf-values (regipy) as written will fail the gate exactly like pe-debug-rich-imports did (import ordlookup). Either widen the allowlist (all are in .venv) or rewrite those goals as stdlib/struct parsers. Also `open` is banned: regipy RegistryHive needs a path -> \n  {\"id\": \"python-pyinstaller-zipapp\", \"concept\": \"Python frozen/runnable packages: PyInstaller CArchive TOC, zipapp .pyz, py2exe/Nuitka markers, pyc versions\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pyinstaller (aliases pyi, python_frozen) on PE/ELF/Mach-O: find cookie `MEI\\\\x0c\\\\x0b\\\\x0a\\\\x0b\\\\x0e` (last occurrence); 2.1+ cookie = magic 8 B, pkg_len u32 BE, toc_offset u32 BE, toc_len u32 BE, pyvers u32 BE (e.g. 311 -> `3.11`), pylib_name 64 B NUL-padded; pkg_start = cookie_end - pkg_len. TOC entries: entry_len u32, data_off u32, cmprsd_len u32, uncmprsd_len u32, cmpr_flag u8, typ\n  {\"id\": \"oci-container-image\", \"concept\": \"Container images: docker-save tarballs and OCI image layouts (Entrypoint/Cmd = where execution begins)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt oci (aliases docker, container, image_tar). tarfile over the member: docker-save has `manifest.json` = [{Config, RepoTags, Layers}] (+ `repositories`); OCI layout has `oci-layout` {imageLayoutVersion}, `index.json` (manifests[].digest/mediaType/annotations `org.opencontainers.image.ref.name`), blobs/sha256/<hex> (manifest -> config digest). Fields from the config JSON: architecture, os, variant, \n  {\"id\": \"electron-asar-npm\", \"concept\": \"Node / Electron runnable packages: app.asar archive header, package.json main/bin/scripts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt asar (alias electron): Chromium Pickle header = u32 LE 4, u32 header_buf_size, u32 pickle payload size, u32 json_len, JSON header {\\\"files\\\": {name: {files:{...}} | {offset: \\\"<decimal str>\\\", size: n, executable?, unpacked?, integrity{algorithm,hash}}}}; file data base = 8 + header_buf_size. Fields: file_names (JSON, depth-first sorted paths), file_count, unpacked_files (JSON), package_name / package_main / pa\n  {\"id\": \"wasm-start-exports\", \"concept\": \"WebAssembly module depth: start function, exports/imports, name and producers custom sections\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt wasm: `\\\\0asm` + version u32 LE 1; section walk (id u8, size LEB128). Fields: section_ids (JSON in order), start_function_index (section 8; absent -> `none`), export_names (JSON file order) + export_kinds (`func`/`table`/`memory`/`global`), has_wasi_start (`_start` export), import_names (JSON `module.field`), import_modules (JSON sorted unique), function_count (section 3), memory_min_pages/max, custom_sect\n  {\"id\": \"jar-signing-osgi-maven\", \"concept\": \"JAR provenance: v1 signature signer, signed vs unsigned entries, OSGi bundle headers, WAR/EAR descriptors, Maven coordinates of nested deps\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt jar: signature_files (JSON), signer_cert_sha256 / signer_subject_cn / signer_serial_hex (reuse lib/meta/prebuilt/apk