{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018jMZbWtMRenKXBjDBiUa1r","type":"tool_result","content":"186\t- Time: GM CORRECT ~29 s after start, 0 wrong (prebuilt hit; worker cross-checked then `--from-solver`). TT 31 fields\n187\t  4.7 s, Mastery 310 = TEN sets 8.0 s, first submit, no generalize; timed .pf were all UNCOMPRESSED SCCA v30.\n188\t\n189\t## GM answer conventions learned\n190\t- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n191\t- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`). Booleans: enum `true` / `false`.\n192\t- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR, video D18): `<width>x<height>`, lowercase `x`, no spaces. Video = ffprobe\n193\t  width/height of v:0 (coded size, NOT rotated, not the tkhd display size).\n194\t- PDF header version: bare `x.y`; absent -> literal `none` (wording; `none` not yet GM-confirmed). Counts: plain integer.\n195\t  Struct sizes with a `_bytes` suffix (D23 page size): the decoded integer in bytes (`1` on disk -> `65536`).\n196\t  Record counts (`evtx.record_count`, D24): number of records actually present (chunk walk), base-10.\n197\t- Registry key names (`registry.hive_root_name`, D25): the root `nk` cell's stored name VERBATIM (case kept, no\n198\t  leading `\\`, no `HKEY_*`/`ROOT` prefix, not the base-block FileName). GM-confirmed in all 3 modes.\n199\t- Prefetch executable name (`prefetch.executable_name`, D26): SCCA header UTF-16LE @16 up to the first NUL, VERBATIM\n200\t  (uppercase as stored, `.EXE` kept, no path, not the `.pf` filename stem, no `-HASH`). GM-confirmed in all 3 modes.\n201\t- JSON lists -- compact, double quotes, no spaces, values SORTED ascending:\n202\t  - `zip.central_directory_member_names`: full stored paths, sorted (D23 TT: CD order REJECTED; D8-22 disk order was sorted).\n203\t  - `ooxml.external_relationship_targets`: Target strings sorted (D15; rels-file order REJECTED).\n204\t  - `macho.cpu_type_set`: `\"0x%08x\"` per slice, deduped, sorted (D20 thin = one element; D23 fat 2-3 slices).\n205\t  - `*-synthesis-<algo>-order`: member names ordered by hex digest ascending (the one ORDER field; `case_insensitive`).\n206\t- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 PE Machine\n207\t  `0x014c`/`0x5064`, u16 ELF e_machine `0x003e`/`0x0102`, u32 AddressOfEntryPoint `0x00065bd0`, u32 Mach-O cputype\n208\t  `0x0100000c` (inside a JSON list, even without `_hex`). Width from the STRUCT / the `_uNN_` in the id; the value from\n209\t  the file's own byte order. (Magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; the binary lane wants `i386` -- different generator.)\n210\t- GUIDs: .NET MVID `Guid.ToString()` lowercase no braces (D12); MSI ProductCode the stored string uppercase WITH braces\n211\t  (D13). Spelling follows the source, not answer_format.\n212\t- Stored strings VERBATIM (no quotes, case kept, delimiters kept): LNK LinkInfo path (D14), PE StringFileInfo value\n213\t  (D11), OOXML Target URL (D15), Message-ID WITH `<>` (D16), Android manifest `package` (D21), JAR `Main-Class` (D22),\n214\t  registry root key name (D25), Prefetch header exe name (D26).\n215\t- Media codec names (`media.*codec_name`): ffprobe `codec_name`: WAV tag 1 -> `pcm_u8`/`pcm_s16le`/`pcm_s24le`/\n216\t  `pcm_s32le` by bits, 3 `pcm_f32le`, 6 `pcm_alaw`, 7 `pcm_mulaw`, 0x55 `mp3`; MP3 `mp3`; Ogg `opus` / `vorbis` (all\n217\t  four GM-accepted D23 timed).\n218\t- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` (D10, unpadded); brace-less MSI GUID (D13); rels-file-order targets (D15); bracket-less\n219\t  Message-ID (D16); `[\"arm64\"]` (D20); CD-order member names (D23); Python repr `['a', 'b']` for any json (D23).\n220\t- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_`, `eocd_total_entries` = the EOCD's own claim, `e_machine`,\n221\t  `page_size`) -- read it literally to pick the structure. A claimed count is NOT a CD walk; CD names are NOT\n222\t  local-header names; `_uNN_hex` fixes read+print width. Header CODES are raw `0x` hex, never tool names.\n223\t\n224\t## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n225\t- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (filename questions: artifact = the zip only). Mastery\n226\t  (most days, all of D15-25): ONE download holding `-01.zip`..`-0N.zip` (D7 three levels; D15-21 five kits, D22 six, D23\n227\t  seven, D24 eight, D25 nine); refs `<set zip> -> <member>`, names reused per set -> resolve by (set zip, member). D9: download\n228\t  `<id>-mastery.zip` vs refs `...-evidence-0N.zip` -> resolve by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`). D6: two\n229\t  same-named downloads -> `delivery N: <zip>` refs. Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt.\n230\t\n231\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n232\t- **Carry-over mutation (D23, 1 wrong TT submit + a Mastery generalize)**: an extractor that only ever saw one sample\n233\t  value is untested. Before a timed run, ask of every carried field \"what if this is the multi-element / other-endian\n234\t  / other-codec case?\" -- fat Mach-O, shuffled CD, Ogg audio, non-x86 PE/ELF machines all arrived the same day.\n235\t- **json list output**: sort + compact `json.dumps` at ONE choke point (D23 Mastery: a local Python list got `str()`'d).\n236\t- **Synthesis dispatch** (lost D15, D16, D17, D19): the timed kit always adds `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-sha256-order`.\n237\t  Start the day's solver from the previous day's solve.py (lane seed `local_answer` + `synthesis_answer` ->\n238\t  `lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order`, artifacts root set INSIDE `_solve_pairs`; Mastery forks one process per set).\n239\t- Registry misses: D14 key one suffix short; D16 fmt `eml` vs GM `email`; D17 `wav.*` vs `media.*`; D21 no `apk` fmt\n240\t  (a new CONTAINER family needs its own fmt word); D25 `regf.root_key_name` existed but GM said `registry.hive_root_name`\n241\t  (domain fmt word + `hive_` prefix) -- grep the lib for the field's last words (`root`+`name`) under every fmt. D22\n242\t  `jar` / D23 `sqlite` prebuilt -> race hits. Check\n243\t  `python3 -c \"import lib.meta as m; print([k for k in m.known_fields() if k[0]=='<fmt>'])\"`, grep\n244\t  `lib/meta/prebuilt/*.py` for the FIELD. D20 substring trap: `cpu_type_set` hit scalar `cpu_type` -> check the SHAPE\n245\t  vs answer_format (`_set`/`_list`/`_names` = a list).\n246\t- Unwired day template (D22): `hctf submit --from-solver` before today's field is dispatched emits literal `none`.\n247\t  Only submit from the solver once `solve.py` prints a real value for EVERY id.\n248\t- Id-slug parsing (D16, 1 wrong): ids repeat the fmt word (`d16-email-001-email-message-id`); anchor `-\\d+-<fmt>-(.+)$`.\n249\t  Never submit `none` without grepping the bytes -- `none` = absent in the artifact, not \"my parser returned None\".\n250\t- Byte order: ELF EI_DATA @5 / the Mach-O magic decide (fat headers ALWAYS BE, slices carry their own magic); SQLite\n251\t  header is ALWAYS big-endian. Fat cputype is in BOTH fat_arch and the slice header -- may disagree in a variant: the\n252\t  set field reads fat_arch. Video geometry has FOUR sources (stsd, SPS crop = ffprobe, tkhd, matrix); trust SPS-cropped.\n253\t- EVTX (D24): count by WALKING records in every chunk (a chunk's free-space offset ends it; slack after it is not a\n254\t  record); header next_record_id is a claim that a dirty/truncated/shortened log can break; a log may hold several\n255\t  chunks and a non-first chunk may be empty or zeroed. EventRecordID gaps = the \"shortened timeline\" sibling.\n256\t- Prefetch (D26): check `MAM` @0 BEFORE looking for `SCCA` @4 -- a compressed .pf has no readable strings. The\n257\t  wrapper may come or go between modes (D26 single compressed, timed plain): branch on the magic, never on the mode.\n258\t  Version (17/23/26/30/31) moves run count and last-run slots; the name @16 and hash @0x4C are fixed for all.\n259\t- Registry hives (D25): two \"names\" live in the file -- base-block FileName @0x30 (renamed/truncated, last 31 UTF-16\n260\t  chars of the original path) and the root nk name. `root`/`key` fields = the nk; `file_name` fields = @0x30. Offsets\n261\t  in cells are relative to 0x1000 (first hbin); every cell starts with an i32 size, so `nk` sits at 0x1000+off+4.\n262\t- SQLite: page size `1` = 65536 (u16 overflow); WAL (`@18/@19 == 2`) does not change the page size; a truncated or\n263\t  embedded copy keeps a valid header -- read the header of the NAMED member, don't infer from file length.\n264\t- A pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the 409 `start_required` body (questions, NO `answer_ids`); answer under\n265\t  the live ids. Only the named field is graded -- the flavor never widens it.\n266\t- Container-of-containers: a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` reads the OUTER EOCD. Resolve the named member's bytes first\n267\t  (recurse), then parse. Hostile CD names (`../`, dupes) as-is.\n268\t- Decoys: `*-with-bom.txt`, `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF, friendly APK filenames: bytes win. Require the\n269\t  format's magic before any field of that format (else `none`; a jar WITHOUT `Main-Class` is `none`).\n270\t- Timed windows are seconds, mostly GM round-trips (D23 Mastery start 3.2 + download 2.2 + solve 1.3 + submit 2.4 s\n271\t  for 196 fields). Parse in memory, never shell out in-window; decompress each member once, cache by (set zip, member).\n272\t- Tools installed: exiftool, poppler, qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck, zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost,\n273\t  mediainfo, sqlite3 (CLI + python; `sqlite3` module is worker-only, not in the prebuild gate), ImageMagick,\n274\t  readelf/objdump, aapt + apktool/jadx (`source bin/env.sh`), olevba/oleid, olefile, pefile, pyelftools, LnkParse3,\n275\t  dnfile, mutagen, androguard, python-evtx `Evtx` + `evtx_dump.py`, regipy, dissect.util (lzxpress_huffman, lznt1,\n276\t  lzxpress, lz4, lzo; worker-only) (.venv); msitools under tools/msitools; ffmpeg\n277\t  7.0.2 at `tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2` (not on PATH). NOT: ffprobe, sox.\n278\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c997e921-7591-43d7-ab62-2cec08c53d99","uuid":"6f330dbc-d6c5-4d82-a0d6-8895f2a5e393","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:08:43.787Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md","content":"- Time: GM CORRECT ~29 s after start, 0 wrong (prebuilt hit; worker cross-checked then `--from-solver`). TT 31 fields\n  4.7 s, Mastery 310 = TEN sets 8.0 s, first submit, no generalize; timed .pf were all UNCOMPRESSED SCCA v30.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`). Booleans: enum `true` / `false`.\n- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR, video D18): `<width>x<height>`, lowercase `x`, no spaces. Video = ffprobe\n  width/height of v:0 (coded size, NOT rotated, not the tkhd display size).\n- PDF header version: bare `x.y`; absent -> literal `none` (wording; `none` not yet GM-confirmed). Counts: plain integer.\n  Struct sizes with a `_bytes` suffix (D23 page size): the decoded integer in bytes (`1` on disk -> `65536`).\n  Record counts (`evtx.record_count`, D24): number of records actually present (chunk walk), base-10.\n- Registry key names (`registry.hive_root_name`, D25): the root `nk` cell's stored name VERBATIM (case kept, no\n  leading `\\`, no `HKEY_*`/`ROOT` prefix, not the base-block FileName). GM-confirmed in all 3 modes.\n- Prefetch executable name (`prefetch.executable_name`, D26): SCCA header UTF-16LE @16 up to the first NUL, VERBATIM\n  (uppercase as stored, `.EXE` kept, no path, not the `.pf` filename stem, no `-HASH`). GM-confirmed in all 3 modes.\n- JSON lists -- compact, double quotes, no spa