{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jx2i6YZUhpbGvf5jwzYJSn","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D20 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set; D20 solver carried the dispatch forward -> timed first try; the 409 pre-fetch body listed DIFFERENT Files than the live attempt). D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings. D18: Files = note + panel-001.png + installer-001.msi + video-001.mp4; the single worker pre-wired the dispatch -> TT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try. D19: Files = note + document-001.pdf + shortcut-001.lnk + collector-001.elf; the single worker added an ELF extractor but NOT the synthesis branch -> TT and Mastery solver_incomplete -> offline generalize ported D18's branch. 4 of 5 timed days lost this way: the day's solver must start from the previous day's solve.py. D21: Files grew to FIVE names (note + panel png + managed dll + message eml + mobile-001.apk), same list in all 5 Mastery sets, order re-rolled per set -- never assume a count. D22-D23: Files = FIVE names and DIFFER between sets of one \n\n{\"id\": \"timed-carryover-mutations\", \"concept\": \"Timed kits mutate every carried family; json lists must be SORTED\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 TT/Mastery re-rolled values that were constant D13-D22: PE Machine 0x01c0/0x01c2/0x01c4/0x01f0/0x0ebc/0x5064/0x8664, ELF e_machine 0x0003/0x0028/0x002b/0x0102, audio mp3/opus/vorbis/pcm_s16le, video dims arbitrary, Mach-O FAT 2-3 slices (0x7, 0xc, 0x12, 0x01000007, 0x0100000c, 0x01000012, 0x0200000c), shuffled zip CD, PDF 1.0-2.0, BOM true, identity sizes 72-378 B, sqlite page 512-65536. lib answered all values right; the two failures were list ORDER: GM wants zip CD names and macho cpu_type_set SORTED ascending (CD order rejected; fat_arch order != accepted) and a local override returned a Python list -> repr. Action for lib/solver owners: one json choke point (sorted + compact) for every `json` answer except `*-synthesis-*-order`; fixture tests with multi-slice fat, shuffled CD, Ogg Opus/Vorbis, MP3, non-x86 PE/ELF so the next carried family (sqlite) is covered for its mutations too (page size 1 = 65536, WAL header, UTF-16 encodings). D24: the D23 fixes held -- TT 29 / Mastery 232 (8 sets) first try while the kit mutated again: audio `ftyp M4A ` -> aac and `fLaC` -> flac (still named audio-001.wav), Mach-O thin LE-32 `ce fa ed fe` (60 B) -> [\\\"0x0000000c\\\"] beside fat 2-3 slices, PE 0x0266 MIPS16, ELF 0x0016 S390 / 0x00b7 AArch64 / 0x00f3 RISC-V, SQLite page 2048, PDF 1.1/1.6/1.7. Expect EVTX to mutate from D25: \n\n{\"id\": \"crash-memory-dump-headers\", \"concept\": \"Windows crash/memory dumps: minidump MDMP, kernel PAGEDU64/PAGEDUMP, hiberfil -- next Windows DFIR artifact\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt minidump (aliases mdmp, dmp, crashdump, dump): header `MDMP` @0 + version u16 0xa793 @4, implementation u16 @6, NumberOfStreams u32 @8, StreamDirectoryRva u32 @12, CheckSum u32 @16, TimeDateStamp u32 @20 (unix -> ISO Z), Flags u64 @24 (emit `0x%016x`). Directory entries 12 B {StreamType u32, DataSize u32, Rva u32}; stream_types (JSON list of ints in directory order + names ThreadListStream 3, ModuleListStream 4, MemoryListStream 5, ExceptionStream 6, SystemInfoStream 7, Memory64ListStream 9, HandleDataStream 12, MiscInfoStream 15, ThreadInfoListStream 17). SystemInfo: ProcessorArchitecture u16 (0 x86 `0x0000`, 5 ARM, 9 AMD64, 12 ARM64), NumberOfProcessors u8 @+6, ProductType @+7, Major/Minor/Build @+8/+12/+16, CSDVersionRva -> MINIDUMP_STRING (u32 len + UTF-16). ModuleList: count u32 then 108-B MINIDUMP_MODULE {BaseOfImage u64, SizeOfImage u32, CheckSum, TimeDateStamp, ModuleNameRva ...} -> module_names (path verbatim, file order) + main_module (first). Exception stream: exception_code_u32_hex, exception_address. fmt kernel_dump (aliases crashdump, memory_dump): `PAGEDU64` (64-bit; MachineImageType u32 @0x30, NumberProcessors @0x34, BugCheckCode @0x38 hex, BugCheckParameters u64 x4 @0x40, DumpType u32 @0xf98, SystemTime FILETIME @0xfa8) / `PAGEDUMP` (32-bit offsets @0x2\n\n{\"id\": \"prefetch\", \"concept\": \"Prefetch exe name / run count / last run times / volume info\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt prefetch: executable_name, run_count, last_run_time_utc, format_version, prefetch_hash_u32_hex, volume_serial_u32_hex) + last_run_times_utc (list of 8), volume_device_path, referenced_file_count. Uncompressed SCCA v17/23/26/30 is struct-only; Win10 MAM\\\\x04 needs an LZXpress-Huffman decoder (stdlib port ~120 lines, or tool dissect.util).\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"mft-record\", \"concept\": \"$MFT FILE record $SI vs $FN timestamps, name, parent\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt mft, fields file_name, record_number, parent_record_number, si_created_utc, si_modified_utc, fn_created_utc, fn_modified_utc, timestomp_suspected, is_directory, resident_data_hex_16. Apply update-sequence fixups first.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"gate-allowlist-dfir-libs\", \"concept\": \"Prebuild gate refuses installed DFIR libs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS lacks Evtx, regipy, olefile, oletools, dnfile, LnkParse3, lief, cryptography, asn1crypto, dpkt, PIL, sqlite3, wave, ordlookup. Targets evtx-records (python-evtx) and regf-values (regipy) as written will fail the gate exactly like pe-debug-rich-imports did (import ordlookup). Either widen the allowlist (all are in .venv) or rewrite those goals as stdlib/struct parsers. Also `open` is banned: regipy RegistryHive needs a path -> use a struct nk/vk walker.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"tool-dfir-parsers\", \"concept\": \"Prefetch / MFT / MSG / archive libs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install dissect.util (LZXpress Huffman for Win10 prefetch), python-registry, extract_msg, py7zr, rarfile, pycdlib, analyzeMFT, windowsprefetch. apt: genisoimage (isoinfo), libscca-utils (sccainfo), osslsigncode.\"}\n\n{\"id\": \"eventlog-exports-legacy-evt\", \"concept\": \"Event-log 'reports': Event Viewer CSV/XML/text exports and legacy .evt logs\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D24 flavor 'bundled with reports'. fmt evt (alias legacy_evt): ELF_LOGFILE_HEADER (HeaderSize u32 0x30 @0, `LfLe` @4, major/minor @8/@12 = 1/1, StartOffset @16, EndOffset @20, CurrentRecordNumber @24, OldestRecordNumber @28, MaxSize @32, Flags @36 (1 DIRTY, 2 WRAP, 4 LOGFULL, 8 ARCHIVE), Retention @40, EndHeaderSize @44); records: Length u32 @0, `LfLe` @4, RecordNumber @8, TimeGenerated u32 epoch @12, TimeWritten @16, EventID u32 @20 (low 16 bits = displayed id), EventType u16 @24, NumStrings @26, EventCategory @28, StringOffset @36, UserSid len/off @40/@44, SourceName + Computername UTF-16 @56; EOF record `11111111 22222222 33333333 44444444`. Fields: record_count (walk, wrap-aware from StartOffset), oldest_record_number, current_record_number, next_record_number, is_dirty, event_ids, source_names, computer_names, first/last time_generated_utc. fmt eventlog_report (aliases csv_report, xml_report, report): Event Viewer CSV (header `Level,Date and Time,Source,Event ID,Task Category`), Get-WinEvent/Export-Csv (`TimeCreated`,`Id`,`ProviderName`,`RecordId`), wevtutil XML `<Events><Event xmlns=\\\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/win/2004/08/events/event\\\">`, wevtutil text `Event[N]:` blocks -> record_count, record_ids (sorted JSON), event_ids, first/last time, computer_names, missing_record_ids. Cross-file: repor\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nRanking (D25 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D26-D28 question with no extractor or a lane-wide failure mode.\nD24 EVTX -> D25 registry hive = a WINDOWS DFIR block with DOMAIN fmt words (`registry`, not `regf`). Priority 1:\nthe next DFIR artifacts (crash/memory dumps, ETW `.etl`, CustomDestinations; prefetch / $MFT / USN / ESE / Amcache /\nrecycle bin / jump lists are built), the `registry` fmt-word mirror for the carried hive family, plus the timed\ncarry-over notes. EVTX flavor siblings dropped to 2 (EVTX lasted one day like every family since D17); registry\nflavor siblings (hive identity / host grouping / planted hive) enter at 2.\nTARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c997e921-7591-43d7-ab62-2cec08c53d99","uuid":"96503b07-ee0b-4202-b44d-3788544ff318","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:09:59.140Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D20 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set; D20 solver carried the dispatch forward -> timed first try; the 409 pre-fetch body listed DIFFERENT Files than the live attempt). D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings. D18: Files = note + panel-001.png + installer-001.msi + video-001.mp4; the single worker pre-wired the dispatch 