{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQuSUqzwjEHcpWzQ7BuT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DrFjJt3xNG137JPRboDVkD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'\nt=open(p).read()\ni=t.index('## Readiness gaps')\nm=re.search(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',t[i:],re.S)\njs,je=i+m.start(1),i+m.end(1)\ng=json.loads(m.group(1))\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='prefetch']\nby={x['id']:x for x in g}\nby['timed-carryover-mutations']['detail']+=\" D26: TT 31 / Mastery 310 (10 sets) first try; the NEW family's wrapper flipped between modes (single MAM\\\\x04-compressed prefetch, every timed .pf plain SCCA v30) -- branch on magic, never on mode. Expect D27+ timed kits to mutate prefetch (other SCCA versions 17/23/26/31, MAM with CRC, compressed in timed) and registry (root cell not @0x20, UTF-16 root names) -- see prefetch-carryover-variants.\"\nby['synthesis-siblings']['detail']+=\" D26: still sha256 + FIVE names (note + {evidence-drop-001.zip | document-001.pdf} + document-15-001.docx + macos-001.bin + trace-001.pf), pdf/zip swapped between Mastery sets; Mastery identity ids also differ per set (7 of 21 asked).\"\nby['tool-dfir-parsers']['detail']+=\" D26: dissect.util (lzxpress_huffman, lznt1, lzxpress, lz4, lzo) is now present in .venv -- worker cross-check only (not in the prebuild gate).\"\nby['eventlog-exports-legacy-evt']['detail']+=\" Attempt 1 (D26 night) failed the gate on `import csv` -- split CSV lines by hand (quoted-field regex) and keep stdlib struct/xml.etree only.\"\nfor k in ('crash-memory-dump-headers','etl-etw-trace','customdestinations-ms','registry-domain-fmt-spellings','regf-dirty-translogs','regf-values'):\n    if k in by: by[k]['priority']=2\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"prefetch-carryover-variants\",\"concept\":\"Prefetch as a CARRIED timed family: every SCCA version and MAM wrapper the kit may mutate into\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 single was MAM\\\\x04-compressed, timed plain SCCA v30 -- the wrapper flips between modes, so D27+ timed kits will likely mutate `trace-001.pf`. fmt prefetch (aliases pf, scca), keep every existing field name and make it version-general: v17 (XP/2003: file info 68 B @84, last run FILETIME @0x78, run count @0x90), v23 (Vista/7: last run @0x80, run count @0x98), v26 (8.1: 8 last runs @0x80, run count @0xD0), v30 BOTH layouts (220-B file info: run count @0xD0; 212-B 'variant 2': @0xC8 -- pick by metrics array offset @84 = 0x130 vs 0x128), v31 (Win11 24H2+: parse as v30, choose layout the same way) and an unknown version (still answer executable_name / prefetch_hash / file_size from the fixed header). MAM wrapper: type low nibble 4 = Xpress-Huffman with and without CRC flag 0x80 (CRC32 u32 @8 computed over the header with the CRC field zeroed + payload; stream @12), multi-64-KiB-block streams, type 2 LZNT1 and type 3 plain LZ77 Xpress (decode rather than answering none). Name edge cases: 29-char names with no NUL inside the 60-B field, lowercase/mixed-case stored names kept verbatim, non-ASCII UTF-16. New fields: file_size_bytes (u32 @12), header_file_size_matches (bool vs decompressed length), executable_name_length, compression_format (`xpress_huffman`/`lznt1`/`xpress`/`none`), uncompressed_size_bytes (u32 @4 of MAM). Fixtures: synthesize one .pf per version + a CRC MAM from the libscca spec and assert every field.\"},\n {\"id\":\"prefetch-path-hash-fullpath\",\"concept\":\"Prefetch identity beyond the header name: full exe path, path-hash recompute, filename-hash check, directories, all volumes\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 flavor 'even after filenames changed ... recover executable identities'. fmt prefetch fields: executable_path (the filename-strings entry -- section B offset u32 @100 / size @104 in the file info, UTF-16LE NUL-separated -- whose basename == header name, verbatim e.g. `\\\\VOLUME{01d7...-a1b2c3d4}\\\\WINDOWS\\\\SYSTEM32\\\\CMD.EXE`), executable_directory, filename_strings_count, directory_strings (per volume: offset/count in the volume entry; JSON sorted), directory_count, volume_serials / volume_device_paths / volume_creation_times_utc (every volume entry; serial `0x%08x`), filename_hash_from_name (the `-XXXXXXXX` of a `NAME-XXXXXXXX.pf` member name, emitted `0x` + lowercase; `none` when renamed like `trace-001.pf`), filename_stem_matches_header (bool), computed_path_hash_u32_hex (SCCA hash of the device-form path `\\\\DEVICE\\\\HARDDISKVOLUME<n>\\\\...` upper-cased UTF-16LE: Vista/7 = `h=314159; for byte: h=(h*37+byte) & 0xffffffff`, XP and the Win8+ '2008' 8-byte-block variant per the libscca 'Prefetch hash' doc), path_hash_matches (bool vs header u32 @0x4C). Hosting/ hosted path flags (`\\\\SYSTEM32\\\\DLLHOST.EXE`, `RUNDLL32.EXE`, `MMC.EXE` hash includes the command line) -> note only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"prefetch-host-synthesis\",\"concept\":\"Cross-trace synthesis: connect prefetch traces to hosts and executables\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 flavor 'connect execution traces to the correct hosts'. Over several .pf members (maybe with .lnk / .evtx / .hiv siblings): host key = (volume serial, volume device path, volume creation time) of the first volume; questions like `*-synthesis-host-groups` (JSON list of sorted member-name lists, groups sorted by first name), `*-synthesis-same-host-as-<member>`, `*-synthesis-renamed-traces` (filename stem != header exe name), `*-synthesis-last-run-order` (members by newest last-run FILETIME), `*-synthesis-odd-host` (the trace whose volume differs). Link evidence: LNK LinkInfo VolumeID DriveSerialNumber + TrackerDataBlock MachineID (NetBIOS), EVTX Computer, hive ComputerName -- a prefetch volume serial equals the 32-bit volume serial in LNK VolumeID and the low 32 bits of the NTFS VBR serial. Register in lib.meta.synthesis beside digest_order; parse each set's own Files list.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ntfs-boot-sector-vbr\",\"concept\":\"Filesystem/disk boot structures: NTFS $Boot VBR, FAT/exFAT VBR, MBR partition table, GPT header\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Next DFIR layer below $MFT (built) and the 'host' link for prefetch/LNK volume serials. fmt ntfs (aliases vbr, boot_sector, ntfs_boot, filesystem): require `NTFS    ` @3 + 0x55AA @0x1FE; bytes_per_sector u16 @0x0B, sectors_per_cluster u8 @0x0D (>=0x80 -> 2^(256-v)), cluster_size_bytes, media_descriptor_u8_hex @0x15, total_sectors u64 @0x28, mft_cluster_number u64 @0x30, mftmirr_cluster_number u64 @0x38, mft_record_size_bytes (i8 @0x40: negative -> 2^-v bytes else v*cluster), index_record_size_bytes (i8 @0x44), volume_serial_number_u64_hex @0x48 (`0x%016x`) + volume_serial_u32_hex (low 32 bits, `0x%08x`) + volume_serial_dir_style (`XXXX-XXXX` upper, as `dir`/`vol` print the low 32 bits). fmt fat (FAT12/16: serial u32 @0x27, label 11 B @0x2B, fs type @0x36; FAT32 `FAT32   ` @0x52: serial @0x43, label @0x47) and exfat (`EXFAT   ` @3: partition offset u64 @0x40, volume length @0x48, serial u32 @0x64, fs revision u16 @0x68 -> `1.00`, bytes-per-sector shift @0x6C, cluster shift @0x6D). fmt mbr (aliases partition_table, disk): 0x55AA @0x1FE, disk_signature_u32_hex @0x1B8, 4 entries @0x1BE x16 B {status @0, type u8 @4, lba_start u32 @8, sector_count u32 @12} -> partition_count (non-zero type), partition_types (JSON `0x%02x` in table order), active_partition_index, first_partition_lba; type 0xEE = protective -> fmt gpt: `EFI PART` @512 (LBA1), revision u32 @+8, header size @+12, disk_guid @+56 (mixed-endian -> lowercase canonical; also upper), partition_entry_lba u64 @+72, entry count u32 @+80, entry size @+84; entries {type GUID, unique GUID, first/last LBA, attrs, name UTF-16LE 72 B} -> partition_names, partition_type_guids. A raw disk image (`.img`/`.dd`/`.raw`/`.001`) starting with an MBR: route by 0x55AA + plausible table, then the VBR at first_partition_lba*512.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ntfs-logfile-indx\",\"concept\":\"NTFS $LogFile restart/record pages and $I30 INDX directory index records (incl. slack)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt logfile (aliases ntfs_logfile, $logfile): `RSTR` restart pages (multi-sector header: update-seq offset u16 @4, count @6 -> apply fixups; chkdsk LSN u64 @8, system page size u32 @16, log page size u32 @20, restart area offset u16 @24, minor/major version i16 @26/@28; restart area: current LSN u64 @0, log clients u16 @8, file size u64 @0x18) and `RCRD` pages (last LSN u64 @8, flags @16, page count @20, next record offset @24) -> current_lsn, log_page_size_bytes, system_page_size_bytes, rcrd_page_count, last_end_lsn. fmt indx (aliases i30, index_record, ntfs_index): `INDX` @0, fixups, VCN u64 @16, index header @24 (entries offset u32, index length, allocated size, flags); entries {file reference u64 (record 48 bits + seq 16), entry len u16 @8, key len u16 @10, flags @12, $FILE_NAME key @16: parent ref, C/M/MFT-mod/A FILETIMEs, alloc/real size, flags, name len u8 @+64, namespace @+65, UTF-16 name @+66} -> entry_names (sorted, de-dup DOS 8.3 namespace 2 unless asked), entry_count, slack_entry_names (carved past index length = deleted-file evidence), per-name times. Fixups first or names straddling sector ends break.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ese-catalog-srum\",\"concept\":\"ESE catalog walk: table names, SRUM / WebCache / Windows Search content\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"ese-edb-header (built) covers the header only. fmt ese (aliases edb, jet, srum, webcache): page size from header u32 @236; page n at (n+1)*page_size; page header (Win7+ 80-byte large-page variant when page size >= 16 KiB) flags u32 (root 0x1, leaf 0x2, parent 0x4, empty 0x8, space tree 0x20, index 0x40, long value 0x80, new record format 0x2000); tags at page end (2 x u16 per tag; 15-bit values on small pages). Catalog = FDP 2 starting at page 4 (MSysObjects): leaf records with fixed columns ObjidTable i32, Type u16 (1 table, 2 column, 3 index, 4 long value), Id, ColtypOrPgnoFDP, SpaceUsage, Flags, PagesOrLocale; variable column Name. Fields: table_names (sorted JSON, MSys* included only if asked), table_count, column_names_<table>, table_record_count via the table's FDP leaf walk. SRUM (SRUDB.dat): known table GUIDs {D10CA2FE-6FCF-4F6D-848E-B2E99266FA89} App Resource Usage, {973F5D5C-1D90-4944-BE8E-24B94231A174} Network Usage, {DD6636C4-8929-4683-974E-22C046A43763} Network Connectivity, {5C8CF1C7-7257-4F13-B223-970EF5939312} App Timeline, SruDbIdMapTable (IdType, IdIndex, IdBlob: UTF-16 app path or SID) -> srum_app_names (sorted), srum_tables_present. WebCacheV01.dat: Containers table Name/Directory. Pure stdlib struct; tagged-column decoding only for the few fields named.\"},\n {\"id\":\"windows-text-dfir-artifacts\",\"concept\":\"Text-shaped Windows DFIR artifacts: WER Report.wer, Defender MPLog / DetectionHistory / quarantine, PSReadLine history, setupapi.dev.log\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt wer (aliases report_wer, windows_error_report): UTF-16LE (BOM) INI-like `Key=Value` lines: Version, EventType (APPCRASH, BEX64, ...), EventTime (decimal FILETIME -> ISO Z), ReportIdentifier/IntegratorReportIdentifier (GUID verbatim), AppSessionGuid, Sig[N].Name/Sig[N].Value (Application Name, Application Version, Fault Module Name, Exception Code `c0000005`), NsAppName, AppName, AppPath, OriginalFilename, TargetAppId -> fields by key name snake_cased (app_name, app_path, event_type, fault_module_name, exception_code). fmt defender (aliases mplog, windows_defender): MPLog-*.log lines (`Threat`/`DETECTION`/`SDN` events, ThreatName, file paths after `file:`), DetectionHistory binary (GUID-named files, UTF-16 strings: threat name, resource path, process), quarantine `Entries\\\\{GUID}` + `ResourceData` RC4-encrypted with the well-known 256-byte Defender key (public in the defender-dump / dissect sources) -> detection_name, original_path, detection_time_utc. fmt psreadline (aliases consolehost_history, powershell_history): ConsoleHost_history.txt lines (backtick continuations) -> command_count, last_command, first_command, commands_matching (URL/download cradle). fmt setupapi (setupapi.dev.log): `>>>  [Device Install (Hardware initiated) - USBSTOR\\\\Disk&Ven_...]` + `>>>  Section start YYYY/MM/DD HH:MM:SS.mmm` -> usb_device_ids (sorted), first_install_time per device (local time, verbatim). No csv module (gate).\"},\n {\"id\":\"linux-dfir-logs\",\"concept\":\"Linux DFIR binaries: systemd journal files, utmp/wtmp/btmp, lastlog\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"A plausible post-Windows DFIR turn (host identity = machine id). fmt journald (aliases journal, systemd_journal): signature `LPKSHHRH` @0, compatible_flags u32 @8, incompatible_flags u32 @12 (bit0 XZ, bit1 LZ4, bit2 keyed hash, bit3 ZSTD, bit4 compact), state u8 @16 (0 offline, 1 online, 2 archived), file_id @24, machine_id @40 (16 B -> 32 lowercase hex, the 'host'), tail_entry_boot_id @56, seqnum_id @72, header_size u64 @88, arena_size u64 @96; counters (n_objects, n_entries, head/tail entry seqnum, head/tail entry realtime in us since 1970 -> ISO Z) follow per the systemd JOURNAL_FILE_FORMAT doc -- read their offsets from the doc, gate them on header_size. fmt utmp (aliases wtmp, btmp): 384-B records (glibc x86-64): ut_type i16 @0 (1 RUN_LVL, 2 BOOT_TIME, 5 INIT, 6 LOGIN, 7 USER_PROCESS, 8 DEAD_PROCESS), pid i32 @4, line 32 B @8, id 4 B @40, user 32 B @44, host 256 B @76, exit @332, session i32 @336, tv_sec i32 @340, tv_usec @344, addr_v6 16 B @348 -> record_count, user_names (sorted unique), hosts, boot_count, first/last login time, logins_for_<user>. fmt lastlog: 292-B records indexed by UID {time i32, line 32 B, host 256 B}.\"},\n {\"id\":\"memory-image-headers\",\"concept\":\"Memory acquisition formats beyond Windows crash dumps: LiME, AVML, VMware vmss/vmsn/vmem, VirtualBox core\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"crash-memory-dump-headers (built) covers MDMP / PAGEDU64 / hiberfil. fmt lime (aliases memory_image): range headers magic 0x4C694D45 (`EMiL` on disk) u32 @0, version u32 @4 (1), start u64 @8, end u64 @16 (inclusive), reserved 8 B, then (end-start+1) bytes -> range_count (walk), total_size_bytes, first_range_start_hex, ranges (JSON `0x%x-0x%x`). fmt avml: `AVML` magic + version u32 + start/end u64 + snappy-framed blocks (header only). fmt vmware_state (vmss/vmsn): magic u32 0xbed2bed0 / 0xbad1bad1 / 0xbed3bed3, group count u32 @8, 80-B group entries {name 64 B, offset u64, size u64} -> group_names (file order), has_memory_group. VirtualBox `VBCORE` ELF core note. A raw `.vmem`/`.raw` has no header -> only identity fields.\"},\n {\"id\":\"macos-dfir-artifacts\",\"concept\":\"macOS DFIR artifacts: .DS_Store, FSEvents, unified log tracev3 header\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt ds_store (aliases dsstore): `00 00 00 01` + `Bud1` @4, root block offset u32 @8 (+4 bias), size @12; buddy allocator TOC `DSDB` -> B-tree of records {filename: u32 length + UTF-16BE, structure id 4 ASCII (`Iloc`, `bwsp`, `lsvp`, `modD`, `ptbL`, `vSrn`), type 4 ASCII (`long`/`shor`/`bool`/`blob`/`type`/`ustr`/`comp`/`dutc`)} -> file_names (sorted unique; reveals deleted/renamed folder contents), record_count, structure_ids. fmt fsevents: gzip members, each page `1SLD`/`2SLD`/`3SLD` + unknown u32 + page length u32; records = NUL-terminated path + event id u64 + flags u32 (+ node id u64 on v2/v3, + extra u32 on v3) -> record_count, paths (sorted), flag names per FSEventStreamEventFlags. fmt tracev3 (unified log): chunk header {tag u32 0x1000 header, subtag, length u64}, header chunk: continuous time, boot UUID, timezone path, build -> boot_uuid, header_build. Plus `.plist` already prebuilt.\"}\n]\nfor x in new: assert x['id'] not in by, x['id']\ng=g+new\ng.sort(key=lambda x:x['priority'])  # stable: keeps relative order within a priority\ntxt=json.dumps(g,indent=None,ensure_ascii=False)\nout=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+\"\\n]\"\njson.loads(out)\nt=t[:js]+out+t[je:]\n# ranking text\na=t.index(\"Ranking (D25 post-run)\"); b=t.index(\"TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail`\")\nt=t[:a]+'''Ranking (D26 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D27-D29 question with no extractor or a lane-wide failure mode.\nD24 EVTX -> D25 registry -> D26 prefetch = a WINDOWS DFIR block, DOMAIN fmt words, one artifact per day. Most DFIR\nartifacts are already built (MFT, USN, ESE header, Amcache/ShimCache, recycle bin, jump lists, CustomDestinations,\nETL, minidump, thumbcache, Timeline/BITS/WMI, task XML), so priority 1 = the unbuilt layer under them (filesystem\nboot sectors / partition tables) and making the newly CARRIED prefetch family survive timed mutation (D26 already\nflipped compressed -> plain between modes). Prefetch flavor siblings (path hash / host grouping), $LogFile/INDX, ESE\ncatalog, WER/Defender text artifacts and Linux DFIR at 2; macOS DFIR and memory images at 3. Built D25 priority-1\nDFIR items moved to 2 (they stay built; the prebuild drains only unbuilt `prebuild` gaps).\n'''+t[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\nt=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md').read()\ni=t.index('## Readiness gaps'); m=re.search(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',t[i:],re.S); g=json.loads(m.group(1))\ns=json.load(open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json'))\nkeys={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'}\nassert all(set(x)==keys for x in g)\nids=[x['id'] for x in g]; assert len(ids)==len(set(ids))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not ((s.get('metadata-forensics:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok')) or s.get('metadata-forensics:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g), 'pending', len(pend), pend)\nprint([ (x['priority'],x['id']) for x in g if x['priority']==1])\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6567,"cache_read_input_tokens":141456,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6567},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c997e921-7591-43d7-ab62-2cec08c53d99","uuid":"a30a884e-d828-4f9d-b9dd-85fee77ecf3b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:12:34.688Z","request_id":"req_011CgQuSUXehvAnn43setdFV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DrFjJt3xNG137JPRboDVkD":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'\nt=open(p).read()\ni=t.index('## Readiness gaps')\nm=re.search(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',t[i:],re.S)\njs,je=i+m.start(1),i+m.end(1)\ng=json.loads(m.group(1))\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='prefetch']\nby={x['id']:x for x in g}\nby['timed-carryover-mutations']['detail']+=\" D26: TT 31 / Mastery 310 (10 sets) first try; the NEW family's wrapper flipped between modes (single MAM\\\\x04-compressed prefetch, every timed .pf plain SCCA v30) -- branch on magic, never on mode. Expect D27+ timed kits to mutate prefetch (other SCCA versions 17/23/26/31, MAM with CRC, compressed in timed) and registry (root cell not @0x20, UTF-16 root names) -- see prefetch-carryover-variants.\"\nby['synthesis-siblings']['detail']+=\" D26: still sha256 + FIVE names (note + {evidence-drop-001.zip | document-001.pdf} + document-15-001.docx + macos-001.bin + trace-001.pf), pdf/zip swapped between Mastery sets; Mastery identity ids also differ per set (7 of 21 asked).\"\nby['tool-dfir-parsers']['detail']+=\" D26: dissect.util (lzxpress_huffman, lznt1, lzxpress, lz4, lzo) is now present in .venv -- worker cross-check only (not in the prebuild gate).\"\nby['eventlog-exports-legacy-evt']['detail']+=\" Attempt 1 (D26 night) failed the gate on `import csv` -- split CSV lines by hand (quoted-field regex) and keep stdlib struct/xml.etree only.\"\nfor k in ('crash-memory-dump-headers','etl-etw-trace','customdestinations-ms','registry-domain-fmt-spellings','regf-dirty-translogs','regf-values'):\n    if k in by: by[k]['priority']=2\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"prefetch-carryover-variants\",\"concept\":\"Prefetch as a CARRIED timed family: every SCCA version and MAM wrapper the kit may mutate into\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 single was MAM\\\\x04-compressed, timed plain SCCA v30 -- the wrapper flips between modes, so D27+ timed kits will likely mutate `trace-001.pf`. fmt prefetch (aliases pf, scca), keep every existing field name and make it version-general: v17 (XP/2003: file info 68 B @84, last run FILETIME @0x78, run count @0x90), v23 (Vista/7: last run @0x80, run count @0x98), v26 (8.1: 8 last runs @0x80, run count @0xD0), v30 BOTH layouts (220-B file info: run count @0xD0; 212-B 'variant 2': @0xC8 -- pick by metrics array offset @84 = 0x130 vs 0x128), v31 (Win11 24H2+: parse as v30, choose layout the same way) and an unknown version (still answer executable_name / prefetch_hash / file_size from the fixed header). MAM wrapper: type low nibble 4 = Xpress-Huffman with and without CRC flag 0x80 (CRC32 u32 @8 computed over the header with the CRC field zeroed + payload; stream @12), multi-64-KiB-block streams, type 2 LZNT1 and type 3 plain LZ77 Xpress (decode rather than answering none). Name edge cases: 29-char names with no NUL inside the 60-B field, lowercase/mixed-case stored names kept verbatim, non-ASCII UTF-16. New fields: file_size_bytes (u32 @12), header_file_size_matches (bool vs decompressed length), executable_name_length, compression_format (`xpress_huffman`/`lznt1`/`xpress`/`none`), uncompressed_size_bytes (u32 @4 of MAM). Fixtures: synthesize one .pf per version + a CRC MAM from the libscca spec and assert every field.\"},\n {\"id\":\"prefetch-path-hash-fullpath\",\"concept\":\"Prefetch identity beyond the header name: full exe path, path-hash recompute, filename-hash check, directories, all volumes\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 flavor 'even after filenames changed ... recover executable identities'. fmt prefetch fields: executable_path (the filename-strings entry -- section B offset u32 @100 / size @104 in the file info, UTF-16LE NUL-separated -- whose basename == header name, verbatim e.g. `\\\\VOLUME{01d7...-a1b2c3d4}\\\\WINDOWS\\\\SYSTEM32\\\\CMD.EXE`), executable_directory, filename_strings_count, directory_strings (per volume: offset/count in the volume entry; JSON sorted), directory_count, volume_serials / volume_device_paths / volume_creation_times_utc (every volume entry; serial `0x%08x`), filename_hash_from_name (the `-XXXXXXXX` of a `NAME-XXXXXXXX.pf` member name, emitted `0x` + lowercase; `none` when renamed like `trace-001.pf`), filename_stem_matches_header (bool), computed_path_hash_u32_hex (SCCA hash of the device-form path `\\\\DEVICE\\\\HARDDISKVOLUME<n>\\\\...` upper-cased UTF-16LE: Vista/7 = `h=314159; for byte: h=(h*37+byte) & 0xffffffff`, XP and the Win8+ '2008' 8-byte-block variant per the libscca 'Prefetch hash' doc), path_hash_matches (bool vs header u32 @0x4C). Hosting/ hosted path flags (`\\\\SYSTEM32\\\\DLLHOST.EXE`, `RUNDLL32.EXE`, `MMC.EXE` hash includes the command line) -> note only.\"},\n {\"id\":\"prefetch-host-synthesis\",\"concept\":\"Cross-trace synthesis: connect prefetch traces to hosts and executables\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 flavor 'connect execution traces to the correct hosts'. Over several .pf members (maybe with .lnk / .evtx / .hiv siblings): host key = (volume serial, volume device path, volume creation time) of the first volume; questions like `*-synthesis-host-groups` (JSON list of sorted member-name lists, groups sorted by first name), `*-synthesis-same-host-as-<member>`, `*-synthesis-renamed-traces` (filename stem != header exe name), `*-synthesis-last-run-order` (members by newest last-run FILETIME), `*-synthesis-odd-host` (the trace whose volume differs). Link evidence: LNK LinkInfo VolumeID DriveSerialNumber + TrackerDataBlock MachineID (NetBIOS), EVTX Computer, hive ComputerName -- a prefetch volume serial equals the 32-bit volume serial in LNK VolumeID and the low 32 bits of the NTFS VBR serial. Register in lib.meta.synthesis beside digest_order; parse each set's own Files list.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ntfs-boot-sector-vbr\",\"concept\":\"Filesystem/disk boot structures: NTFS $Boot VBR, FAT/exFAT VBR, MBR partition table, GPT header\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Next DFIR layer below $MFT (built) and the 'host' link for prefetch/LNK volume serials. fmt ntfs (aliases vbr, boot_sector, ntfs_boot, filesystem): require `NTFS    ` @3 + 0x55AA @0x1FE; bytes_per_sector u16 @0x0B, sectors_per_cluster u8 @0x0D (>=0x80 -> 2^(256-v)), cluster_size_bytes, media_descriptor_u8_hex @0x15, total_sectors u64 @0x28, mft_cluster_number u64 @0x30, mftmirr_cluster_number u64 @0x38, mft_record_size_bytes (i8 @0x40: negative -> 2^-v bytes else v*cluster), index_record_size_bytes (i8 @0x44), volume_serial_number_u64_hex @0x48 (`0x%016x`) + volume_serial_u32_hex (low 32 bits, `0x%08x`) + volume_serial_dir_style (`XXXX-XXXX` upper, as `dir`/`vol` print the low 32 bits). fmt fat (FAT12/16: serial u32 @0x27, label 11 B @0x2B, fs type @0x36; FAT32 `FAT32   ` @0x52: serial @0x43, label @0x47) and exfat (`EXFAT   ` @3: partition offset u64 @0x40, volume length @0x48, serial u32 @0x64, fs revision u16 @0x68 -> `1.00`, bytes-per-sector shift @0x6C, cluster shift @0x6D). fmt mbr (aliases partition_table, disk): 0x55AA @0x1FE, disk_signature_u32_hex @0x1B8, 4 entries @0x1BE x16 B {status @0, type u8 @4, lba_start u32 @8, sector_count u32 @12} -> partition_count (non-zero type), partition_types (JSON `0x%02x` in table order), active_partition_index, first_partition_lba; type 0xEE = protective -> fmt gpt: `EFI PART` @512 (LBA1), revision u32 @+8, header size @+12, disk_guid @+56 (mixed-endian -> lowercase canonical; also upper), partition_entry_lba u64 @+72, entry count u32 @+80, entry size @+84; entries {type GUID, unique GUID, first/last LBA, attrs, name UTF-16LE 72 B} -> partition_names, partition_type_guids. A raw disk image (`.img`/`.dd`/`.raw`/`.001`) starting with an MBR: route by 0x55AA + plausible table, then the VBR at first_partition_lba*512.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ntfs-logfile-indx\",\"concept\":\"NTFS $LogFile restart/record pages and $I30 INDX directory index records (incl. slack)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt logfile (aliases ntfs_logfile, $logfile): `RSTR` restart pages (multi-sector header: update-seq offset u16 @4, count @6 -> apply fixups; chkdsk LSN u64 @8, system page size u32 @16, log page size u32 @20, restart area offset u16 @24, minor/major version i16 @26/@28; restart area: current LSN u64 @0, log clients u16 @8, file size u64 @0x18) and `RCRD` pages (last LSN u64 @8, flags @16, page count @20, next record offset @24) -> current_lsn, log_page_size_bytes, system_page_size_bytes, rcrd_page_count, last_end_lsn. fmt indx (aliases i30, index_record, ntfs_index): `INDX` @0, fixups, VCN u64 @16, index header @24 (entries offset u32, index length, allocated size, flags); entries {file reference u64 (record 48 bits + seq 16), entry len u16 @8, key len u16 @10, flags @12, $FILE_NAME key @16: parent ref, C/M/MFT-mod/A FILETIMEs, alloc/real size, flags, name len u8 @+64, namespace @+65, UTF-16 name @+66} -> entry_names (sorted, de-dup DOS 8.3 namespace 2 unless asked), entry_count, slack_entry_names (carved past index length = deleted-file evidence), per-name times. Fixups first or names straddling sector ends break.\"},\n {\"id\":\"ese-catalog-srum\",\"concept\":\"ESE catalog walk: table names, SRUM / WebCache / Windows Search content\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"ese-edb-header (built) covers the header only. fmt ese (aliases edb, jet, srum, webcache): page size from header u32 @236; page n at (n+1)*page_size; page header (Win7+ 80-byte large-page variant when page size >= 16 KiB) flags u32 (root 0x1, leaf 0x2, parent 0x4, empty 0x8, space tree 0x20, index 0x40, long value 0x80, new record format 0x2000); tags at page end (2 x u16 per tag; 15-bit values on small pages). Catalog = FDP 2 starting at page 4 (MSysObjects): leaf records with fixed columns ObjidTable i32, Type u16 (1 table, 2 column, 3 index, 4 long value), Id, ColtypOrPgnoFDP, SpaceUsage, Flags, PagesOrLocale; variable column Name. Fields: table_names (sorted JSON, MSys* included only if asked), table_count, column_names_<table>, table_record_count via the table's FDP leaf walk. SRUM (SRUDB.dat): known table GUIDs {D10CA2FE-6FCF-4F6D-848E-B2E99266FA89} App Resource Usage, {973F5D5C-1D90-4944-BE8E-24B94231A174} Network Usage, {DD6636C4-8929-4683-974E-22C046A43763} Network Connectivity, {5C8CF1C7-7257-4F13-B223-970EF5939312} App Timeline, SruDbIdMapTable (IdType, IdIndex, IdBlob: UTF-16 app path or SID) -> srum_app_names (sorted), srum_tables_present. WebCacheV01.dat: Containers table Name/Directory. Pure stdlib struct; tagged-column decoding only for the few fields named.\"},\n {\"id\":\"windows-text-dfir-artifacts\",\"concept\":\"Text-shaped Windows DFIR artifacts: WER Report.wer, Defender MPLog / DetectionHistory / quarantine, PSReadLine history, setupapi.dev.log\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt wer (aliases report_wer, windows_error_report): UTF-16LE (BOM) INI-like `Key=Value` lines: Version, EventType (APPCRASH, BEX64, ...), EventTime (decimal FILETIME -> ISO Z), ReportIdentifier/IntegratorReportIdentifier (GUID verbatim), AppSessionGuid, Sig[N].Name/Sig[N].Value (Application Name, Application Version, Fault Module Name, Exception Code `c0000005`), NsAppName, AppName, AppPath, OriginalFilename, TargetAppId -> fields by key name snake_cased (app_name, app_path, event_type, fault_module_name, exception_code). fmt defender (aliases mplog, windows_defender): MPLog-*.log lines (`Threat`/`DETECTION`/`SDN` events, ThreatName, file paths after `file:`), DetectionHistory binary (GUID-named files, UTF-16 strings: threat name, resource path, process), quarantine `Entries\\\\{GUID}` + `ResourceData` RC4-encrypted with the well-known 256-byte Defender key (public in the defender-dump / dissect sources) -> detection_name, original_path, detection_time_utc. fmt psreadline (aliases consolehost_history, powershell_history): ConsoleHost_history.txt lines (backtick continuations) -> command_count, last_command, first_command, commands_matching (URL/download cradle). fmt setupapi (setupapi.dev.log): `>>>  [Device Install (Hardware initiated) - USBSTOR\\\\Disk&Ven_...]` + `>>>  Section start YYYY/MM/DD HH:MM:SS.mmm` -> usb_device_ids (sorted), first_install_time per device (local time, verbatim). No csv module (gate).\"},\n {\"id\":\"linux-dfir-logs\",\"concept\":\"Linux DFIR binaries: systemd journal files, utmp/wtmp/btmp, lastlog\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"A plausible post-Windows DFIR turn (host identity = machine id). fmt journald (aliases journal, systemd_journal): signature `LPKSHHRH` @0, compatible_flags u32 @8, incompatible_flags u32 @12 (bit0 XZ, bit1 LZ4, bit2 keyed hash, bit3 ZSTD, bit4 compact), state u8 @16 (0 offline, 1 online, 2 archived), file_id @24, machine_id @40 (16 B -> 32 lowercase hex, the 'host'), tail_entry_boot_id @56, seqnum_id @72, header_size u64 @88, arena_size u64 @96; counters (n_objects, n_entries, head/tail entry seqnum, head/tail entry realtime in us since 1970 -> ISO Z) follow per the systemd JOURNAL_FILE_FORMAT doc -- read their offsets from the doc, gate them on header_size. fmt utmp (aliases wtmp, btmp): 384-B records (glibc x86-64): ut_type i16 @0 (1 RUN_LVL, 2 BOOT_TIME, 5 INIT, 6 LOGIN, 7 USER_PROCESS, 8 DEAD_PROCESS), pid i32 @4, line 32 B @8, id 4 B @40, user 32 B @44, host 256 B @76, exit @332, session i32 @336, tv_sec i32 @340, tv_usec @344, addr_v6 16 B @348 -> record_count, user_names (sorted unique), hosts, boot_count, first/last login time, logins_for_<user>. fmt lastlog: 292-B records indexed by UID {time i32, line 32 B, host 256 B}.\"},\n {\"id\":\"memory-image-headers\",\"concept\":\"Memory acquisition formats beyond Windows crash dumps: LiME, AVML, VMware vmss/vmsn/vmem, VirtualBox core\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"crash-memory-dump-headers (built) covers MDMP / PAGEDU64 / hiberfil. fmt lime (aliases memory_image): range headers magic 0x4C694D45 (`EMiL` on disk) u32 @0, version u32 @4 (1), start u64 @8, end u64 @16 (inclusive), reserved 8 B, then (end-start+1) bytes -> range_count (walk), total_size_bytes, first_range_start_hex, ranges (JSON `0x%x-0x%x`). fmt avml: `AVML` magic + version u32 + start/end u64 + snappy-framed blocks (header only). fmt vmware_state (vmss/vmsn): magic u32 0xbed2bed0 / 0xbad1bad1 / 0xbed3bed3, group count u32 @8, 80-B group entries {name 64 B, offset u64, size u64} -> group_names (file order), has_memory_group. VirtualBox `VBCORE` ELF core note. A raw `.vmem`/`.raw` has no header -> only identity fields.\"},\n {\"id\":\"macos-dfir-artifacts\",\"concept\":\"macOS DFIR artifacts: .DS_Store, FSEvents, unified log tracev3 header\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"fmt ds_store (aliases dsstore): `00 00 00 01` + `Bud1` @4, root block offset u32 @8 (+4 bias), size @12; buddy allocator TOC `DSDB` -> B-tree of records {filename: u32 length + UTF-16BE, structure id 4 ASCII (`Iloc`, `bwsp`, `lsvp`, `modD`, `ptbL`, `vSrn`), type 4 ASCII (`long`/`shor`/`bool`/`blob`/`type`/`ustr`/`comp`/`dutc`)} -> file_names (sorted unique; reveals deleted/renamed folder contents), record_count, structure_ids. fmt fsevents: gzip members, each page `1SLD`/`2SLD`/`3SLD` + unknown u32 + page length u32; records = NUL-terminated path + event id u64 + flags u32 (+ node id u64 on v2/v3, + extra u32 on v3) -> record_count, paths (sorted), flag names per FSEventStreamEventFlags. fmt tracev3 (unified log): chunk header {tag u32 0x1000 header, subtag, length u64}, header chunk: continuous time, boot UUID, timezone path, build -> boot_uuid, header_build. Plus `.plist` already prebuilt.\"}\n]\nfor x in new: assert x['id'] not in by, x['id']\ng=g+new\ng.sort(key=lambda x:x['priority'])  # stable: keeps relative order within a priority\ntxt=json.dumps(g,indent=None,ensure_ascii=False)\nout=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+\"\\n]\"\njson.loads(out)\nt=t[:js]+out+t[je:]\n# ranking text\na=t.index(\"Ranking (D25 post-run)\"); b=t.index(\"TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail`\")\nt=t[:a]+'''Ranking (D26 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D27-D29 question with no extractor or a lane-wide failure mode.\nD24 EVTX -> D25 registry -> D26 prefetch = a WINDOWS DFIR block, DOMAIN fmt words, one artifact per day. Most DFIR\nartifacts are already built (MFT, USN, ESE header, Amcache/ShimCache, recycle bin, jump lists, CustomDestinations,\nETL, minidump, thumbcache, Timeline/BITS/WMI, task XML), so priority 1 = the unbuilt layer under them (filesystem\nboot sectors / partition tables) and making the newly CARRIED prefetch family survive timed mutation (D26 already\nflipped compressed -> plain between modes). Prefetch flavor siblings (path hash / host grouping), $LogFile/INDX, ESE\ncatalog, WER/Defender text artifacts and Linux DFIR at 2; macOS DFIR and memory images at 3. Built D25 priority-1\nDFIR items moved to 2 (they stay built; the prebuild drains only unbuilt `prebuild` gaps).\n'''+t[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\nt=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md').read()\ni=t.index('## Readiness gaps'); m=re.search(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',t[i:],re.S); g=json.loads(m.group(1))\ns=json.load(open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json'))\nkeys={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'}\nassert all(set(x)==keys for x in g)\nids=[x['id'] for x in g]; assert len(ids)==len(set(ids))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not ((s.get('metadata-forensics:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok')) or s.get('metadata-forensics:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g), 'pending', len(pend), pend)\nprint([ (x['priority'],x['id']) for x in g if x['priority']==1])\nEOF"}}}
